If a clinician considers a new-drug-prescription for a patient and the patient takes a current-medication then the clinician should review the current-medication before the new-drug-prescription.
If a clinician considers a new-drug-prescription for a patient and the patient takes an over-the-counter-drug then the clinician should review the over-the-counter-drug before the new-drug-prescription.
If a clinician considers a new-drug-prescription for a patient and the patient takes a natural-remedy then the clinician should review the natural-remedy before the new-drug-prescription.
